Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Framesleuth depends on, but does not vendor, the packages declared in
pyproject.toml. Each is installed from PyPI under its own license and retains
its own copyright. The ones worth calling out because they carry native code or
non-permissive terms:

  PyAV (av)            BSD-3-Clause. Ships prebuilt wheels that BUNDLE FFmpeg
                       binaries. FFmpeg is LGPL-2.1-or-later (and GPL if a
                       build enables GPL components). This is why Framesleuth
                       needs no system ffmpeg — and it means anyone
                       REDISTRIBUTING a Framesleuth bundle, container image, or
                       frozen binary is redistributing FFmpeg too, and must
                       satisfy the LGPL themselves. Running the agent locally
                       from source, which is the normal path, does not trigger
                       that obligation.

  opencv-python        Apache-2.0. Wheels bundle OpenCV, which includes
                       third-party components under BSD and other permissive
                       terms; see the LICENSE-3RD-PARTY file in the installed
                       distribution.

  faster-whisper       MIT. Runs CTranslate2 (MIT). Model weights are NOT
                       covered by this notice — whichever Whisper model you
                       download carries its own license.

  FastAPI, Starlette,  MIT / BSD-3-Clause.
  Pydantic, uvicorn,
  aiohttp, aiosqlite,
  mcp

Model weights are never distributed with Framesleuth. The vision and coder
models you point it at are obtained and licensed by you.
